PARABOLIC CYLINDER FUNCTIONS (693)
At x=0,
19.17.4  \overline{W}(a,0)=\frac{1}{2^{1}}|\frac{\Gamma(\tfrac{1}{4}+\tfrac{1}{2}ia)}{\Gamma(\tfrac{3}{4}+\tfrac{1}{2}ia)}|^{n}-\frac{1}{2^{1}}\sqrt{\frac{G_{1}}{G_{3}}}\]
19.17.5  \overline{W}'(a,0)=-\frac{1}{2^{1}}|\frac{\Gamma(\tfrac{3}{4}+\tfrac{1}{2}ia)}{\Gamma(\tfrac{1}{4}+\tfrac{1}{2}ia)}|^{n}-\frac{1}{2^{1}}\sqrt{\frac{G_{3}}{G_{1}}}\] Complex Solutions
19.17.6  \underline E(a,x)=k^{-1}W(a,x)+ik^{1}W(a,-x)
19.17.7  \underline E^{n}(a,x)=k^{-1}W(a,x)-ik^{1}W(a,-x)
where
19.17.8  \underline k=\sqrt{1+e^{2\pi a}}e^{\tau a}\qquad 1/\underline k=\sqrt{1+e^{2\pi a}}+e^{\tau a}\] In terms of  \underline U(a,x)\) of 19.3,
19.17.9  \underline E(a,x)=\sqrt{2}e^{1\pi a+i\nu+1\sigma_2}U(ia,xe^{-1\tau s}) with
19.17.10  \phi_2=\arg\Gamma(\tfrac{1}{2}+ia) where the branch is defined by \phi_2=0 when \ a=0 and by continuity elsewhere.
Also
19.17.11  \sqrt{2\pi U(ia,xe^{-1\mu i})}=\Gamma(\tfrac{1}{2}-ia)'[e^{1\mu a-1\mu i}U(-ia,xe^{1\mu})+e^{-1\mu i\nu}U(-ia,-xe^{1\mu\gamma})]
19.18. Wronskian and Other Relations
19.18.1  \underline W(\{W(a,x),W(a,-x)\}=1
19.18.2  \underline W(\{E(a,x),E^{n}(a,x)\}=-2i
19.18.3  \sqrt{1+e^{2\pi a}E(a,x)}=e^{\tau a}E^{n}(a,x)+iE^{n}(a,-x)
19.18.4  \underline E^{n}(a,x)=e^{-i(\phi_3+1\nu)}E(-a,ix)
19.18.5  \sqrt{\Gamma(\tfrac{1}{2}+ia)}E^{n}(a,x)=e^{-1\mu i}\sqrt{\Gamma(\tfrac{1}{2}-ia)}E(-a,ix)
19.19. Integral Representations
These are covered for 19.1.3 as well as for 19.1.2 in 19.5 (general complex argument).
